            <div xml:id="ch1">

                <pb facs="0113" n="1" sameAs="frus:frus1935v03/pg1"/>

                <head>Chapter I: January 1–April 5, 1935</head>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>Resumption of postal services between China and “Manchoukuo”; Japanese
                        military encroachment on Chahar territory; Japanese diplomatic campaign to
                        overcome Chinese objections to policy of “cooperation” with Japan; Finance
                        Minister Kung’s report on “grave situation”, February 1; China’s declaration
                        on Soviet sale of Chinese Eastern Railway to “Manchoukuo”, March 16; Japan’s
                        withdrawal from League of Nations, March 27; British decision to dispatch
                        technical financial expert to China, March 28; Ambassador Grew’s report on
                        Soviet sale of Chinese Eastern Railway to “Manchoukuo”, April 5</p>
                </quote>











































































































